## Bootstrap

```bash
git clone {{ polity_layout.meta_repo_url or "git@github.com:emsenn/561.git" }}
cd {{ polity_layout.short or "561" }}
vcs import . < polity.yaml             # clones every member repo into its slot
./dev.sh                                # enter the devshell with local sibling overrides
```

Without `vcstool`, you can read `polity.yaml` and `git clone` each repo manually into its declared path.

`./dev.sh` enters the Nix devshell rooted at the polity. It applies `--override-input` for every sibling that exists locally, so editing a member repo (e.g. `platforms/agential-orchestration/pyfars/`) is reflected immediately in the devshell. Without an override, the devshell uses the pinned commit from `flake.lock`.

For day-to-day work in the meta-repo, prefer `./dev.sh` over bare `nix develop`. Use bare `nix develop` when you intentionally want the pinned flake inputs without local member overrides.

