## Tooling

`pyfars` ({{ pyfars_verb_count }} registered verbs, paired with {{ skill_count }} engineering skills) is the polity's substrate CLI. Enter the polity's devshell (`nix develop .#<computer-system>` or plain `nix develop`) to get it on `PATH`.

Common operations:

- `pyfars validate` — run all validation rules against the corpus.
- `pyfars stats` — corpus health overview.
- `pyfars show <slug>` — pretty-print a note plus its in/out edges.
- `pyfars search "<query>" --bm25` — ranked text + frontmatter search.
- `pyfars context <slug> --depth 2` — bounded subgraph from a slug for LLM context.
- `pyfars where <kind> <slug>` — suggest the canonical directory for a new note.
- `pyfars install-harness` — list / install / uninstall harnesses (this file is generated by one).
- `pyfars audit-commits` — bind commits to task records as substrate witnesses.

See the [pyfars repository's README](https://github.com/emsenn/pyfars#readme) for the full toolkit guide.

